{% comment %}
  Walterin · Questions about THIS product.

  Replaces the general FAQ that used to sit on every product page (Veronka,
  8 Oct 2026). "Where do you send it", "What can I pay with" and "Can I send it
  back" are the same answers on all three pages and they belong on /pages/faq —
  a product page should answer the things you want to know before buying THAT
  thing, and then get out of the way.

  Same component as the FAQ page: the accordion, WalterinBold for the heading,
  the question in body text. No new design objects.

  The questions are chosen per product handle below, and their words live in
  locales/*.json under walterin.product_faq, for the same reason the FAQ page's
  do: the Slovak is versioned with the theme and cannot be half-written.

  ONLY TRUE FACTS. Every answer here is checked against
  docs/WALTERIN-GROUND-TRUTH.md — 80 cards in the box, 84 × 138 mm, 180 pages,
  129 × 207 mm softcover, 30 stickers on two sheets — or against the Terms
  (six downloads, no DRM). No quantities, no stock, nothing about an edition
  size. A product with no entry below renders nothing at all, which is the
  correct behaviour: silence beats an invented answer.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign handle = product.handle
  assign keys = ''
  case handle
    when 'tarot'
      assign keys = 'box,lang,size,know'
    when 'walterin-prague'
      assign keys = 'formats,ebook,lang,pages'
    when 'stickers'
      comment
        One question, because one fact is all we have. Veronka, 8 Oct: "only
        what we know (30 stickers on two sheets), nothing invented."
      endcomment
      assign keys = 'what'
  endcase
-%}

{%- if keys != blank -%}
  {%- assign key_list = keys | split: ',' -%}
  <div class="wui-scope wui-faq wui-product-faq">
    <div class="wui-wrap">
      <div class="wui-product-faq__head">
        <h2 class="wui-product-faq__title wui-label">{{ 'walterin.product_faq.title' | t }}</h2>
        <a class="wui-product-faq__all" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: '/pages/faq' | replace: '//', '/' }}">
          {{- 'walterin.product_faq.all' | t -}}
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="wui-accordions">
        {%- for key in key_list -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign base = 'walterin.product_faq.q.' | append: handle | append: '_' | append: key
            assign q_text = base | append: '.q' | t
            assign a_text = base | append: '.a_html' | t
            assign anchor = 'pq-' | append: handle | append: '-' | append: key
          -%}
          {%- unless q_text contains 'Translation missing' -%}
            <details class="wui-accordion" id="{{ anchor }}" data-wui-acc>
              <summary>
                <span class="wui-accordion__title">
                  <h3 class="wui-faq__q">{{ q_text }}</h3>
                </span>
                <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </summary>
              <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
                <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">{{ a_text }}</div>
              </div>
            </details>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product questions",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Three to five questions about this product only. Which questions appear is chosen by product handle in the section file; the words are in the theme's language files under walterin.product_faq. A product with no entry shows nothing. The general questions — shipping, payment, returns — live on the FAQ page, which this section links to."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Product questions" }]
}
{% endschema %}
